2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> >
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> > If you go this route, note that perl also contains a complete bzip2
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> > implementation. Since there has been concern, over a recent change
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> > proposed to tar, to only care about what's in base, we might want to
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> > add libbzip2 to base and link the perl module against it... (to be
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> > considered post-release)
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |>
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> And how many days or hours before someone says I want bzip2 support in
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> the bootblocks also (without any consideration their proposal blows up
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> 50% of the media, and will require a very significant amount of
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> development/test process).
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |>
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> I don't know why we limited ourselves to netinet. We should bring back
2024-11-16T13:51:41 |> netiso. People should be able to depend upon is to supply them with
